body:
Ship the remastered label sheet as high-resolution art. User, 2026-11-25:
- "upscaled remastered version will need resized"
- "These should replace the existing"
- "Make sure we get a better sprite-rect so we're not chopping off parts"
- "I also don't want to ship the same sized version - I want an upscaled version which will look good on all resolutions"

Asset: working/classic_ui/hd/interface.pak-001_x4.png (1848x288, the user's) is a 4x remaster of staged/client/sprites/interface/sprite_fonts/002.png (462x72, InterfaceSprFonts, 40 frames).

Uses today (verified 2026-11-25):
- the magic and magic shop dialogs draw frames 19-29 (the circle-number strip and roman numerals);
- frames 30-39 are GameFont::Numbers, the HUD HP and MP digits (dialog_box_hud_panel.cpp:92-115);
- frames 0-18 are the old character labels.

The remaster has NO digits: frames 30-39 are blank in it. Keep the old digits, upscaled, or replace the Numbers font separately.

Measured on a 1x trial (reverted, not shipped):
- the remaster's ink runs past 30 of the 40 old rects, by up to 3 px per side at 1x;
- refitting each rect to the ink assigned to it, and shifting the pivot by the same amount, cut nothing off, but 7 pairs of rects then overlap by 1-27 px (up to 9 ink pixels shared). Trial script: .claude/scratch/coordinator/main_menu_wide/refit_rects.py.

Needs: hi-res sprite support. The sprite folder format has no scale field today (sprite_folder.cpp, verified by grep), so frames always draw at their pixel size. Proposal:
- a per-sprite art scale in the manifest (art px per logical px, here 4);
- the loader divides rects and pivots by it;
- the draw uses smooth filtering, so the sheet renders sharp at every output resolution.
Rects are refit on the 4x sheet so no glyph is clipped and neighbours do not bleed.

**Done when:**
- sprite_fonts 002 ships at 4x with refit rects;
- the magic and magic shop numerals and the HUD digits draw correctly at 1x, 1.6x and fullscreen;
- no glyph is clipped (a census of ink outside each rect reads 0);
- both builds are clean.

Source: user in chat, 2026-11-25.
